(364, 'Incident Report – Jeanne (Kimironko) Laptop Diagnosis & Tablet Theft', 'Incident', '<p><strong>Dear ED,</strong></p><p>After Jeanne’s tablet, which she used for invoicing and the EBM system, was stolen, I tested whether her current POS printer could work with her laptop, but all attempts failed. \r\nAs a result, she’s unable to generate invoices or access the EBM, leading to significant delays.</p><p><strong>Here are possible solutions: </strong> </p><p>Short-term: Supply a Windows-compatible POS printer for her laptop.  </p><p>Preferred: Provide Jeanne with a Windows OS tablet that supports a SIM card, allowing her to use just the tablet and a Bluetooth POS printer, no laptop required, fully portable.  </p><p>The theft has been reported to the authorities.\r\n\r\n</p><p>Kind regards  </p>', '2026-04-16', '2026-04-17', 2, '2026-04-17 10:49:08', '2026-04-17 10:49:08', '11:00:00', '17:00:00', 'RWVCA Head Office');
