(706, 'Recurring EBM Tablet Failure (Staff: Odile, Gatsibo Site)', 'Incident', '<p><strong>Dear ED,</strong></p><p>Below is the incident report regarding the issue of the tablet used for EBM activities by Gatsibo field staff member, Odile.</p><h3><strong>1. Overview</strong></h3><p>Odile, a field staff member at the Gatsibo site, has raised the same issue many times over an extended period: her tablet, used for EBM invoicing, shuts down unexpectedly and frequently, especially when trying to generate an invoice. This has caused significant delays in invoicing and financial losses.</p><h3><strong>2. Previous Interventions &amp; Failures</strong></h3><p>Our team and the Rwanda Revenue Authority (RRA) have attempted multiple fixes:</p><ul><li>Reboot (advised by RRA): <strong>Failed</strong></li><li>Formatting (advised by RRA): <strong>Failed</strong></li><li>Diagnostic &amp; maintenance: <strong>Failed again</strong></li><li>RRA recommendation to replace tablet: <strong>Delayed; tablet continued failing</strong></li></ul><p>After any temporary fix, the tablet works for&nbsp;less than two minutes&nbsp;before shutting down again. The problem remains completely unsolved.</p><h3><strong>3. Proposed Next Step: Using a Laptop</strong></h3><p>Installing EBM on a laptop could be considered, but this option can be rejected due to:</p><ul><li><strong>Conflict with daily work:</strong>&nbsp;The laptop is already needed for QuickBooks, RWVCA Portal reporting, and other activities. Running EBM on it would likely cause application shutdowns.</li><li><strong>Penalty risk:</strong>&nbsp;If the EBM application is deleted or goes missing from the laptop, the RRA imposes a&nbsp;200,000 RWF fine.</li></ul><h3><strong>4. Consequences</strong></h3><ul><li>Delayed invoice generation</li><li>Financial losses for the site</li><li>Repeated frustration for Odile</li><li>Risk of RRA sanctions</li></ul><h3><strong>5. Recommended Solution</strong></h3><ul><li>Stop attempting repairs on the faulty tablet immediately.</li><li>Provide Odile with a&nbsp;new Windows OS tablet that supports a SIM card, paired with a&nbsp;Bluetooth POS printer, no laptop required, fully portable.</li></ul><h3><strong>6. Summary &amp; Request</strong></h3><p>In all, Odile\'s EBM tablet at the Gatsibo site has failed repeatedly despite multiple RRA-guided repairs (reboot, format, maintenance). It now works for less than two minutes per attempt. Using a laptop risks a 200,000 RWF penalty and conflicts with her daily reporting tasks. The only viable solution is to replace the faulty tablet with a new Windows OS tablet (SIM-capable) and a Bluetooth POS printer.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Kind Regards,</strong></p>', '2026-06-01', '2026-06-02', 2, '2026-06-02 16:39:13', '2026-06-02 16:39:13', '17:00:00', '18:00:00', 'RWVCA Head Office'),
(707, 'Daily report', 'Other', '<p><br></p>', '2026-06-02', '2026-06-02', 81, '2026-06-02 19:10:45', '2026-06-02 19:10:45', '21:08:00', '21:08:00', 'BUGESERA'),
(708, 'KUGARAGAZA ISHUSHO YUKO IMASHINI IHAGAZE/ IMEZE NYUMA YO KUVA KU MUSUPPLIER', 'Activity', '<b>Mwiriwe neza Logistic (Emmy),<br></b>Ndizera mu meze neza,<br>Nifuzaga gutanga ishusho ngari y\'iyi mashini (laptop-<b>HP ELITEBOOK 830 G6</b>) ifite SN# 5CG01524PQ na nimero iranga igikoresho ariyo&nbsp;<b>&nbsp;MRO-LPT-006</b>&nbsp;mwari mwampaye ngo ikorerwe isuzumwa niba ikora neza cyangwa se ntakindi kibazo ifite nyuma yuko ivuye ku musupplier wari wazitanze kuri RWVCA nyuma ikaza kugira ikibazo.<br>Ubu imashini irako neza, tugendeye ku isuzuma ryakozwe ritandukanye, harimo kuba ifata murandasi, kub ayihuta mu mikorere, kuba isohora amajwi neza, kuba ibika kandi yinjiza umuriro, kuba na software issues zihari, ndetse amadrivers akaba arimo kandi akora.<br><br>Murakoze.', '2026-06-02', '2026-06-02', 2, '2026-06-03 12:31:56', '2026-06-03 12:31:56', '09:00:00', NULL, 'RWVCA Head Office'),
